{"type":"text","text":"Four fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, and A→E — are each narrowed by 3\/16 of the syntonic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"comma, equal to (3\/2)·(80\/81)^(3\/16) ≈ 697.923 cents. Four more fifths — E→B,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"B→F♯, B♭→F, and F→C — are each narrowed by (¼ PC − 3\/16 SC) ≈ 1.833 cents,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"equal to (3\/2)·(81\/80)^(3\/16)·(2¹⁹\/3¹²)^(−1\/4) ≈ 700.122 cents. The remaining","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"four fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Published in "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" 90 (1800).","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/youngI"},"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types.","type":"text"}],"title":"IvorTuning","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"abstract":[{"text":"A tuning system in which all twelve keys are usable but have distinct tonal characters,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"achieved by distributing the Pythagorean comma unevenly around the circle of fifths.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WellTemperament"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"WellTemperament"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","title":"WellTemperament"